course: dictionary
lesson: 10415
title: Context clues: trimmer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trimmer is a tool or machine that cuts things neatly, such as hedges, grass edges, hair or a beard. The word can also mean a person who trims things. «Power tools such as drills, saws and hedge trimmers cut and crush in an instant.» The word tools is a clue: the sentence lists drills and saws as tools, so a hedge trimmer must be one too.
explain: Look at the words in front of trimmer: hedge, beard and nail. Each one tells you what is being trimmed, so the phrase tells you the job. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "a hedge trimmer is a machine that cuts hedges neatly" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Trimmers have sharp, moving blades or fast lines, so they can hurt you. The sentence says they «cut and crush in an instant», which means very quickly. Keep well away from a trimmer while it is in use, never touch its plug, and ask an adult for help.
explain: Words change from place to place. In the UK a grass trimmer is often called a strimmer, and in Australia people say whipper snipper. The tool is the same, so context and the words around it still tell you what is meant.
fact: A trimmer is a tool or machine that cuts things neatly.
fact: A hedge trimmer cuts hedges, a beard trimmer cuts facial hair, and a nail trimmer cuts nails.
fact: «Power tools such as drills, saws and hedge trimmers cut and crush in an instant.» This is why trimmers are dangerous.
fact: Keep away from a trimmer while it is in use, and never touch the plug.
fact: Trimmer can also mean a person who trims things.
exercise: «Power tools such as drills, saws and hedge trimmers cut and crush in an instant.» What is a hedge trimmer? | A kind of garden gate | A plant that grows along the edge of a field | *A machine for cutting hedges neatly | A soft brush for cleaning windows
exercise: Lily says a beard trimmer is a comb for brushing hair. What is a beard trimmer really for? | *Cutting facial hair neatly | Growing a beard faster | Brushing hair into shape | Washing a beard in the bath
exercise: Why should children keep away from a trimmer while it is running? | It makes a pleasant smell | It is too heavy to lift | It needs to be fed grass | *Its sharp moving blades could cause serious harm
test: Which tool is used to cut hair or a beard neatly? | nail file | grass rake | hedge trimmer | *beard trimmer
test: What does the phrase «cut and crush in an instant» suggest about power tools? | *They work very quickly and can be dangerous | They are only used indoors | They work very slowly and gently | They are always made of wood
exam: In «Power tools such as drills, saws and hedge trimmers cut and crush in an instant», what does such as show? | Drills are not really tools | Saws are always gentle | *Hedge trimmers are one example of power tools | Trimmers are the slowest tools of all
